# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Xingyu Guo et al. (2026). Benchmarking Universal Machine Learning Interatomic Potentials for Alkali-Ion Battery Kinetics.
#   ACS Materials Letters. doi:10.1021/acsmaterialslett.6c00134  arXiv:2601.10938v1
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2601.10938v1 (sha256 a0fd525bb5ef63b6...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 199 (Dataset/benchmark). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
#
# Encoding scope: bibliographic facts only. The paper benchmarks 23
# pretrained universal MLIPs (M3GNet, CHGNet, MACE, Orb, MatterSim, GRACE
# and SevenNet families) zero-shot against DFT for Li+ and Na+ migration
# barriers in electrode materials and for ion diffusivities and
# structural correlations in solid electrolytes. It trains no model and
# its errors are on derived kinetic quantities. Read from the arXiv
# preprint (v1).

