###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - The accuracy figures are MAEs of migration barriers (NEB) against DFT, in meV: M3GNet 638, M3GNet-DIRECT 666, CHGNet 382, MACE (MPTrj) 312, MACE (MPA) 148, MACE (OMat24) 89, GRACE (MPTrj) 190, SevenNet-0 262, Orb-v2 (MPTrj) 267, Orb-v2 (MPA) 348, Orb-v3 models 75 to 111, MatterSim 132. A migration barrier is not an energy, force or stress error of a test set, so schema 0.1.2 has no MetricProperty for it and nothing is encoded. Diffusivity errors are likewise not encodable.
# - Useful for the registry: SI Table S1 pins every benchmarked model to a checkpoint identifier (M3GNet-MP-2021.2.8-PES, M3GNet-MP-2021.2.8-DIRECT-PES, CHGNet-MPtrj-2024.2.13-11M-PES, MACE-MP-0b3, MACE-MPA-0, MACE-OMAT-0, orb-mptraj-only-v2, orb-v2, eight orb-v3 variants, mattersim-v1.0.0-5M, GRACE-2L-MP-r6, GRACE-2L-OMAT-L-base, GRACE-2L-OAM-L, SevenNet-0, SevenNet-omat, SevenNet-MF-ompa). Four of these are registry models already (M3GNet-MPF-2021.2.8, M3GNet-DIRECT, MACE-MP-0b3 medium, MatterSim-v1); with a barrier metric property this paper would link to them directly.
# - Read from the arXiv v1 preprint, whose title differs from the ACS Materials Letters article; arXiv id matched by title and author.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
